{
  "_comment": "Curated niche brands for the Loupe live catalog feed. Each runs on Shopify, which exposes a public /products.json endpoint (no auth). 'currency' is the store's base currency — the scraper converts to USD. 'perBrand' caps how many products are pulled from each brand to keep the catalog curated. To add a brand: confirm https://<domain>/products.json returns JSON, then add an entry. Bot-protected stores (return empty) are simply skipped at runtime. To REMOVE a brand, delete its entry here AND add it to EXCLUDE_BRANDS in build_catalog.py — deleting it here alone lets its items ride the grace-window carry-forward for days and does not stop it re-entering via a multi-brand reseller's vendor field. Removed 2026-07-29: Mackage, Marfa Stance.",
  "fx_to_usd": {
    "USD": 1.0,
    "AUD": 0.66,
    "EUR": 1.08,
    "GBP": 1.27,
    "CAD": 0.73,
    "NZD": 0.61,
    "SEK": 0.092,
    "DKK": 0.145,
    "EGP": 0.02
  },
  "perBrand": 60,
  "_retailers_comment": "PARTNER RETAILERS — real shops we've partnered with that stock many designers. Items keep the DESIGNER as the brand (the taste engine learns designers, not shops) and carry a 'retailer' stamp the app resolves against catalog.retailers for the tile tint, badge and in-app store block. 'productTypes' scopes what we ingest (Loupe is a women's app — a boutique also sells menswear, candles and books). 'perVendorCap' stops one high-volume label eating the whole allocation. Set 'enabled': false to switch a partnership off in one edit — items disappear on the next refresh, no app release needed.",
  "retailers": [
